<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  Burmese (my) — SCAFFOLD ONLY. AWAITING HUMAN TRANSLATION.

  This file deliberately contains NO machine-translated strings. The only
  entries are the two server-load strings at the bottom, whose wording the
  owner chose directly (see the comment there). Its presence is what
  registers Burmese as a locale the watch app can serve: Android resolves
  res/values-my/ automatically when the watch language is Burmese, and any
  string missing from here falls back to res/values/strings.xml (English). So
  today a Burmese watch shows English text, correctly and without crashing,
  and the moment a real translation lands it takes effect with no code change.

  No machine translation has been added and none should be. This app remote-
  controls a VPN for people who may be relying on it for their safety; a
  plausible-looking but wrong "Connected" is worse than an honest English one.

  To translate: copy a <string> element from res/values/strings.xml into this
  file and replace only the text. Keep the name attribute identical and keep
  the %1$s placeholders, with one deliberate exception: do not add an
  app_name entry here AT ALL. app_name is a permanent disguise pinned to the
  same value in every locale this app ships (see the long comment on it in
  res/values/strings.xml) — it is the one string in this file that must
  never be translated, localised, or overridden, in Burmese or any other
  language. An override here would fire only for a watch set to this
  language, which is exactly the population most of this app's users are.

  tools:ignore="MissingTranslation" is on the <resources> element because lint
  is otherwise correct to shout that every string here is missing. That IS the
  current state, it is tracked here in this comment, and the alternative (no
  values-my at all) would leave Burmese unregistered entirely.
-->
<resources xmlns:tools="http://schemas.android.com/tools"
    tools:ignore="MissingTranslation">
    <!--
      OWNER-APPROVED WORDING, not machine translation. The two server-load
      strings below were chosen by the owner directly (Round LC, 2026-09-27):
      .agent/debates/_decisions/owner_ruling_load_bar_burmese_20260927.md.
      The bytes are copied from that ruling (the Flutter app_my.arb carries the
      same text with {percent} instead of %1$d). Every other string in this
      file stays untranslated under the rule in the header above.
    -->
    <string name="watch_server_load_percent">ဆာဗာ အသုံးပြုမှုနှုန်း %1$d%%</string>
    <string name="watch_server_load_unknown">ဆာဗာ ဝန် မရရှိပါ</string>
</resources>
